%I A195984 #59 Oct 02 2026 00:35:36
%S A195984 8,13,22,18,14,13,11,9,6,9,7,7,8,6,8,7,7,6,5,5
%N A195984 The size of the smallest boundary square in the simple perfect squared rectangles of order n.
%C A195984 Ian Gambini showed in his thesis that the minimum value for a(n) is 5. Brian Trial found 3 simple perfect squared rectangles (SPSRs) of order 28 with boundary squares of size 5 in September 2011. An unsolved problem is to find the lowest order SPSR with a '5 on the side'.
%C A195984 Added a(22) = 6 (Stuart Anderson), Brian Trial has found a(28) = 5. This gives an upper bound of 28, in addition to the lower bound of 23, to the problem of finding the lowest order SPSR with a square of size 5 on the boundary. - _Stuart E Anderson_, Sep 29 2011
%C A195984 Found a(23) = 8, the lower bound is now order 24. - _Stuart E Anderson_, Nov 30 2012
%C A195984 Found a(24) = 7, the lower bound is now order 25. - _Stuart E Anderson_, Dec 07 2012
%C A195984 From _Stuart E Anderson_, Sep 26 2026: (Start)
%C A195984 Found a(25) = 7, the lower bound is now order 26.
%C A195984 Found a(26) = 6, the lower bound is now order 27.
%C A195984 Jim Williams found a(27) = 5.  The problem is now solved and 27 is the lowest order for SPSRs with the minimum side of 5.
%C A195984 Brian Trial has found 3 SPSRs in order 28 with a side of 5, so a(28) = 5.
%H A195984 Stuart E. Anderson, <a href="http://www.squaring.net/sq/sr/spsr/spsr_boundary.html">Simple Perfects by Boundary Rules and Conditions</a>.
%H A195984 Stuart Anderson, <a href="http://www.squaring.net/sq/ss/s-pss.html">'Special' Perfect Squared Squares</a>, accessed 2014. - _N. J. A. Sloane_, Mar 30 2014
%H A195984 Stuart Anderson, <a href="http://www.squaring.net/sq/ss/corners/27_441x390-5-side-JW.png">Order 27: 441x390 ; 5 on the side</a> (a(27) has the lowest order SPSR with 5 on the boundary).
%H A195984 Ian Gambini, <a href="http://alain.colmerauer.free.fr/alcol/ArchivesPublications/Gambini/carres.pdf">Quant aux carrés carrelés</a>, Thesis, Université de la Méditerranée Aix-Marseille II, 1999.
%e A195984 a(27) has the lowest order SPSR with 5 on the boundary
%Y A195984 Cf. A002839.
